From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Santiago Palladino <santiago@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:58:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(e2e): sequencer rewards under a per-registry reward
 calculator

Adds multi-node/rewards/registry_reduction_calculator: two EOA-staked and two
ATP-staked validators (one per ATP registry) propose checkpoints with txs under
a RegistryReductionCalculator that zeroes one registry's reward. After every
epoch proof, each coinbase's sequencer rewards on L1 must equal its registry
reward plus the sequencer share of the fees in the proven checkpoints it
proposed.

The e2e setup no longer forces every node's coinbase to the L1 publisher, so a
validator node now defaults to the address of its first validator key and each
single-key validator node accrues rewards at its own address. This drops the
now-redundant clearInheritedCoinbase option.

